  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 6.1.6, package-lock.json packages[\"\"] says 6.1.5.",
        "  make version of ncmake bumps info.xml, composer.json and package.json and re-syncs package-lock.json in one step, so they cannot drift apart. ncmake's lint-version workflow fails a push or a pull request on exactly this drift. The App Store and the server read info.xml, npm and composer read their own manifest. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying more than one version number, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "lint-version/version-drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 32 to 32; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 32 is below the oldest maintained major (33, the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 32 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml, package.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, MIT.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 32 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.4.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^22.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The checks run on another Node: 20 (npm-test.yml). They lint and test the code and build no release asset, so this decides only what those runs see."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.js, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.js), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (phpunit.unit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.js: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "script-without-workflow",
      "lines": [
        "package.json declares the script test, which no installed workflow runs.",
        "  The template node-test of nextcloud/.github runs test: make workflows-install W=node-test",
        "  A check that no workflow runs on a pull request catches only what the contributor who remembers to run it catches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "3 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/typings, @vue/test-utils, @vue/tsconfig.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 762 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "The 9 links of appinfo/info.xml answer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP 8.1 is the floor in appinfo/info.xml and in composer.json, platform 8.1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
